Maintainer direction 2026-11-21: skilletor should run on its Perl binaries everywhere, the way briefing does. POSIX already starts the pinned release binary first, through bin/skilletor-start (k191 activates it with the pin). On Windows, bin/skilletor.exe still starts Node through winlaunch: k169 decided (a) extend winlaunch, (c) Node until then; the winlaunch extension never landed.

briefing has a Windows bootstrap of its own: briefing-bootstrap.c, built reproducibly with build.py. It finds the cached binary under <config>/briefing/bin/<V>/<pin>/, downloads it, checks it against the pinned SHA256SUMS line, warms up PAR, and falls back to Python.

To decide: does skilletor reuse that bootstrap, generalized by name, or get its own? Record on k169 that this supersedes its decision (a)/(c).

Done when: bin/skilletor.exe (or its successor) starts the pinned, cached, checksum-verified release binary on Windows, with a fallback when none is cached; proven natively on Windows (windows-developer board), not only in CI.

Not a blocker for the CPAN release: the plugin's Windows path comes from main.

superseded by hub decision 2026-11-25 (no Perl runtime); removal in k275 on branch getty-bun
